  "id": "autosomal-recessive",
  "term": "autosomal recessive",
  "definition": "Autosomal recessive describes an inherited pattern in which a disorder can appear in children from unaffected parents, as in the reported family with two affected siblings. In this context, it refers to a genetic form of nonsyndromic intellectual disability passed on in that way.",
